SUMMARY:Futures Softball Camp at Penn Medicine Park
DESCRIPTION:ntroduce your little one to the exciting world of softball at our Futures Softball Camp! This fun-filled\, one-day camp is designed for kids ages 4-6\, giving them the perfect opportunity to learn the basics of the game in a playful and engaging environment. Our friendly coaches will guide campers through fun activities and simple drills\, all focused on building a love for the game while developing important early skills like catching\, throwing\, and hitting. \nThe Futures Camp emphasizes enjoyment and teamwork\, making sure every child feels included and confident. With plenty of games\, laughter\, and smiles\, it’s a fantastic way for your young athlete to take their first swing at softball! Whether it’s their first time holding a bat or they’re ready for their first game\, the Futures Camp is the perfect way for your young ballplayer to start their softball journey!  \nJoin us for exciting\, skill-building softball camps where players of all levels will enhance their abilities in every aspect of the game! \nParticipants will focus on key fundamentals such as hitting\, pitching\, fielding\, base running\, and throwing. Through instruction from the Stormers Softball coaching staff and fun drills\, players will progressively build their skills and gain confidence on the field\, setting the foundation for success in competitive play. Train like the Stormers! \nSoftball Camps are run by Jackie Wardrop and Brionna Rinier! \nRuns: 9:00 am – 12:00 Noon \n\nAdditional Fun Things for Kids To Do in Lancaster?\n\n\nSummer Camps\nPetting Zoo\nRailroad Attractions\n\n\n\nFun on the Farm\nAmusement Parks\nMini Golf\n\n\n\nArcades & Video Games\nZip-Lines\nEvents Calendar\n\n \nTake a look at many more Summer Camps offered throughout Lancaster County this summer!
URL:https://lancasterpa.com/events-calendar/futures-softball-camp-penn-medicine-park/
LOCATION:Penn Medicine Park\, 650 North Prince Street\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17603
CATEGORIES:Children & Family events,Community Interest,Lancaster City,Outdoor Activities,Summer Camp
